# The dialogue of Nurse Ana, the contact at the Public Hospital.
# The contact admits the thefts and gives the player one sample to try.
#
# EVERY LINE HERE IS A PLACEHOLDER. Nick owns the lore and the names.
#
# A player on the trail step gets the confession. A player on a later step
# gets the graft reminder. Each other player gets a line that gives nothing
# away.

~ start
if quest.on_step("augmentation_intro", "trail")
	=> trail
elif quest.on_step("augmentation_intro", "graft")
	=> graft
elif quest.on_step("augmentation_intro", "report")
	=> report
{{npc.header}}
{{npc.name}}: [Placeholder: {{npc.name}} is busy dealing with other patients.]
- Placeholder: leave. => END

# The confession. The response fires the talk target. The graft step then
# opens, and its on_enter hook gives the sample.
~ trail
{{npc.name}}: [Placeholder: {{npc.name}} admits that the Hospital takes the augments, out of need, and asks the candidate to understand.]
{{npc.name}}: [Placeholder: {{npc.name}} asks the player to apply the graft to a patient.]
{{npc.name}}: [Placeholder: {{npc.name}} offers one sample, and tells the player how to apply a graft to themselves.]
- Placeholder: take the sample.
	do quest.talk("augmentation_intro", "npc_aug_hospital_1")
	=> graft
- Placeholder: leave. => END

# The graft lesson. No target fires here: the graft command reports the
# graft to the quest engine.
~ graft
{{npc.name}}: [Placeholder: {{npc.name}} explains the graft, and that a Locus can apply it better for more XP.]
{{quest.objectives("augmentation_intro")}}
- Placeholder: try it. => END

~ report
{{npc.name}}: [Placeholder: {{npc.name}} asks what the player will tell the Clinic.]
- Placeholder: leave. => END

~ farewell
{{npc.name}}: [Placeholder farewell of the Hospital contact.]
